Let $\alpha\vdash m$, let $Q\ge0$ be a nonzero operator on $V_\alpha$, and define the probability $$u(g)=\frac{D_\alpha}{m!\mathop{\mathrm{Tr}}Q^2}
             |\mathop{\mathrm{Tr}}(Q\rho_\alpha(g))|^2\quad(g\in S_m).$$ Let $U$ be its average action on strings of length $m$ over four colors. Then $$\mathop{\mathrm{Tr}}U\le\langle\chi_\alpha^2,4^{\#\mathrm{cycles}}\rangle_{S_m}
 =\sum_{\boldsymbol\beta}(c^{\alpha}_{\boldsymbol\beta})^2=C(\alpha).$$

There is an absolute $C$ such that, for every $\alpha\vdash m$ and integer $h\ge1$, $$\label{eq:restriction-cost}
 \log C(\alpha)\le t_h(\alpha)\log4
       +C(1+h)(1+\sqrt{k(\alpha)})\log(2m).$$

If $c^{\lambda}_{\alpha_1,\ldots,\alpha_4}>0$, then for every integer $h\ge1$, $$\label{eq:hook-deficit}
 \sum_i t_h(\alpha_i)\le t_h(\lambda),
 \qquad \sum_i k(\alpha_i)\le k(\lambda).$$

Fix $\delta\in(0,1/2)$ and put $a=1/2-\delta$. For every $H>2$ and $\epsilon>0$, a sufficiently large fixed cutoff $M$ makes every such recursion tree satisfy $$\label{eq:tree-budget}
 \log F(\lambda)\le\epsilon K+
 \frac\theta a\left\{
    R_H(\lambda)+\frac K2\log\frac NK\right\}.$$ The cutoff and all constants in this statement are independent of the final even moment $r$.

Orient $\lambda\vdash N$ so its first row is a longest side, put $K=N-\lambda_1>0$, and let $\zeta=(\lambda_2,\lambda_3,\ldots)\vdash K$. For $H>2$, $$\begin{aligned}
 \log D_\lambda
 &\ge K\log(N/K)+\log D_\zeta-E_{N,K},\label{eq:row-hook}\\
 R_H(\lambda)&\le\log D_\zeta+4K/H,\label{eq:rank-hook}
\end{aligned}$$ where $E_{N,K}=O(K/N)$ for $K<N/3$ and $E_{N,K}=O(\sqrt N\log(2N))$ for $K\ge N/3$. There is also an absolute $c>0$ such that $\log D_\lambda\ge cK$ for all sufficiently large $N$ and every nontrivial, nonsign $\lambda$.
